    {
      "id": "qtm-m5-worked-examples-c1",
      "heading": "Battery life: set-up and test statistic",
      "explanation_md": "**Problem:** a company claims new batteries last **500 hours** (mean). A sample of **n = 25** has a mean of **480 hours**, with a **known population SD of 50 hours**. Test at **α = 0.05**: is there evidence that batteries last **less than** 500 hours?\n\n**Step 1: Hypotheses.**\n\nH0: μ = 500 hours\n\nH1: μ < 500 hours\n\nThe words *less than* make this a **left-tailed** test.\n\n**Step 2: Test statistic.**\n\nz = (x̄ − μ0) / (σ/√n) = (480 − 500) / (50/√25) = −20/10 = **−2.0**",
      "example_ids": [
        "qtm-ex-m5-battery-life"
      ],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Battery: H0: μ = 500, H1: μ < 500; z = (480 − 500)/(50/√25) = −20/10 = −2.0.",
      "clarification": null,
