    {
      "id": "qtm-m5-worked-examples-c4",
      "heading": "Coffee bags: critical values from the t table and the decision",
      "explanation_md": "**Step 4: Critical values.** Using the t-distribution table for **df = 29 at α/2 = 0.025**, the slide takes **critical t-values of ±2.364**.\n\nThe deck's **t table** lists degrees of freedom down the side (1 to 30, then 40 up to 1000 and Infinite) and nine columns across: 0.2, 0.15, 0.1, 0.05, 0.025, 0.01, 0.005, 0.001 and 0.0005. On the **df 29** row, the **0.025** column reads **2.364**.\n\n**Step 5: Decision.** Since **t = −2.19 > −2.364**, the test statistic falls in the **fail to reject region**. **Fail to reject H0.** The slide adds: reject H1; there is sufficient evidence to suggest the mean bag weight **does not differ** from 1 kg.\n\n**Step 6: Interpretation.** The sample suggests the machine fills bags at 1 kg on average, at 5% significance.\n\nNote: the earlier rule in this deck says that when H0 is not rejected we do not say we accept H0.",
      "example_ids": [
        "qtm-ex-m5-coffee-bags"
      ],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Coffee: df 29, α/2 = 0.025, critical t = ±2.364; t = −2.19 > −2.364, so fail to reject H0.",
